ent planning and to  financial futures  um that takes me to well one of the  questions that have come in from the  audience roger has asked us a question  finding a trusted advisor to provide  just advice is hard  rather than um  [Music]  paying the  set fee on assets under management so  what use is an ifa  is an ifa someone you should consult at  the beginning of your retirement  planning and when you've got it in place  you don't need to pay  separately for that advice  you need products as well as advice  where where does the ifa come in how do  you know you've got a good one  well that is a very interesting question  uh because this is an unbelievably  fragmented industry meaning there are  huge numbers of ifas across britain  and  personal finance is a topic which lots  of people find quite difficult to get to  grips with and so  they end up getting themselves into a  situation sometimes where they think  they've got a friend  who is helping advise them you know with  what they need to do but that friend is  actually taking quite a lot of money off  the table for themselves so  um  when you assess whether or not this is  the type of person you want to work with  i think you need first of all to be sure  are they asking the right questions in  terms of really trying to understand  what you're trying to achieve what are  your financial goals they're not trying  to sell you product or not even indeed  their service but they're listening to  what it is you want and they are  completely clear when you ask them  how their costs work which lots if you  ever feel someone isn't being clear  they're almost definitely not and there  will be other things going on  um  the question about advice though is a  very interesting one because  i think that we will all probably have  moments in our life when advice is  necessary so retirement is a classic one  you know as you run up to retirement or  possibly you've just started  it's a good time to have a sort of mark  to market 