ow one of the things that you  may get as a result of that guidance is  now would be a good time to go and see a  financial advisor and then you know  obviously i think uh you want to look at  the range of different uh ways in which  the internet is disrupting uh this this  space as well as  who might be good locally in word of  mouth so um i think i wouldn't add  anything to what charlotte uh has said  except that i would say to uh people  listening that if you think you want to  try  to get some guidance then pension wise  is the one that the government  provides and i think has had some good  feedback but not enough people are using  it  and we might say that the wise friend  you need at certain points decisions  about inheritance gifts and so on may  not be an ifa it may be the family  solicitor  the wise old family friend and so on  let's take it let's take a couple more  questions from the  audience uh  so  uh here's a here's a  rather technical one  um  charlotte what role could equity release  play in retirement planning mark asks is  this one equity release yes um i mean  this is where you're able to take the  value of your property and to you know  um basically  earn  a a pot of money based on the value of  your house that then on in the event  that you die the  the property value will be paid back to  the person that you've effectively  borrowed from  um  we  tend to see relatively little of it  among our clients um so we don't spend a  lot of time advising on it i think that  it's one of those tools which is  good to know is available um i think it  is very important though whenever you're  borrowing money um to think quite hard  about what a you know what actually what  is the charge effectively what do you  what is it costing you because it's all  very well said well once i die i don't  have to worry about it but it may well  be your children's problem or you know  so  i'm  a little bit skeptical um having said  that i can certainly see in some  people's cases it it it's the right  thing to do it it  could i mean this may be an unfair thing  to say harry tell me about right it's  the sort of device that could smack of  miss selling or hard selling one  imagines the equity release  salesman sort of going from door to door  slightly  yeah slightly uncomfortable and also as  a constituency mp you know i have had  some horror stories come through my case  work so i would  ask people to think long and hard and  also ask questions about what interest  rate they would be paying and  compounding at  when they look at equity release  something to be very careful about yeah  i mean generally speaking anything that  sounds too good to be true  is too good to be true and anything that  is suggesting it can return multiples of  the risk-free rate is by definition  going to have deep embedded risk in it  so you know we've seen these mis-selling  problems in the past um and i'm sure  there will be you know hopefully fewer  but nevertheless the same sorts of  problems in the future and it's just  worth remembering you know harriet  mentioned this notion of a free lunch  and there being no free lunch bar  diversification  you know i would say it kind of goes  back to those things of what are the  things you can control versus what are  the things you can't control and really  trying to focus on those bits that you  can so don't sit with piles of cash do  make sure you know exactly how much  you're paying someone in fees and  whether it's the right thing to do do be  diversified you know there are things  that are within our control  what's what's outside is you know when  am i going to die uh are the markets  going to go up or down you know where's  inflation going um and those are more  things that you can model for rather  than control yeah  one more  rather technical one this is from julian  can charlotte comment on salary  sacrifice for additional voluntary  contributions for those on modest  salaries  well actually i think t